<td>$3,000</td>
<td>$2,800</td>
<td>-7%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CPA</td>
<td>$48</td>
<td>$26</td>
<td>-46%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>ROAS</td>
<td>0.8</td>
<td>2.3</td>
<td>+188%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>AOV</td>
<td>$52</td>
<td>$68</td>
<td>+31%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Fatigue complaints</td>
<td>23/week</td>
<td>4/week</td>
<td>-83%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Black Friday hit $127,000 in sales with 2.6 ROAS.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Channels should complement, not compete</strong></li>
<li><strong>Audience quality beats audience quantity</strong></li>
<li><strong>Budget allocation needs continuous optimization, not one-time setup</strong></li>
</ol>
<hr />
<p><strong>Your Action Checklist:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Audit current channel budget split vs. industry benchmarks</li>
<li>[ ] Check audience overlap—split if over 40%</li>
<li>[ ] Enable dayparting or hourly budget rules</li>
<li>[ ] Set daily budget caps to prevent overspend</li>
<li>[ ] Weekly budget reviews, not fire drills</li>
</ul>
